---
title: "TranscryptFormer: pan-calicoblast cosine similarity"
---

## Concept

Calicoblast cells from all species that carry this annotation (Amil, Spis, Ocup,
Gast) are pooled after per-species centering. The mean L2-normalised vector of
this pool is the **pan-calicoblast centroid**. We then compute its cosine
similarity against every cell-type centroid in every comparison species.

A high similarity to a specific cell type in a non-skeletal species suggests a
transcriptional homologue; a diffuse/low pattern suggests this cell identity is
novel to Scleractinia.

